    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d784">

                <pb facs="1072" n="1062" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg1062"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">General Marshall to
                        Colonel James C. Davis
                    </hi><anchor n="58" xml:id="d784-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-12-26">26 December
                        1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1285. Getting in touch with General Johnson for expression of opinion on rapidity
                    with which negotiations can be carried out with the Chinese re 90012. Believe it
                    desirable permit Chinese purchase of these supplies if they are prepared for
                    early decision. You will be notified promptly.</p>
                <p>New subject: I do not desire that transfer to the Chinese of 6 Liberty ships
                    which was under discussion when I departed Washington be delayed by requesting
                    my approval before final consummation. This transfer has my approval.<anchor
                        n="59" xml:id="d784-f2"/>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d784-f1" n="58" type="source" xml:id="d784-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram transmitted through the Adjutant General, War Department.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d784-f2" n="59" xml:id="d784-f2-content">
                <p>The comments of Colonel Davis on this paragraph are included in Department’s
                    telegram No. 2079, December 29, 1945, <ref target="frus1945v07#pg_1200">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1945, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">vii</hi>, p. 1200</ref>. For further
                    correspondence on the transfer of shipping to China, see <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg786">pp. 786</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
